From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] combase: CoGetCallerTID, message filter retries, CoRegisterSurrogate (3760)

CoGetCallerTID and CoRegisterSurrogate were stubs (E_NOTIMPL), and a call
rejected by the callee's message filter was either dropped on the floor
(SERVERCALL_RETRYLATER ran the method anyway) or never offered to the caller's
filter. CoGetCallerTID now names the calling apartment (its thread for an STA,
0 for the MTA, S_FALSE for another process), a call that the callee's
IMessageFilter::HandleInComingCall rejects goes to the caller's
IMessageFilter::RetryRejectedCall, which cancels, retries at once or after a
wait, and CoRegisterSurrogate keeps the process's ISurrogate. CORE review
(patches/notes/3760.txt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS
---
diff --git a/dlls/combase/combase.c b/dlls/combase/combase.c
index e4cc077..785096c 100644
--- a/dlls/combase/combase.c
+++ b/dlls/combase/combase.c
@@ -3621,8 +3621,27 @@ HRESULT WINAPI CoTestCancel(void)
  */
 HRESULT WINAPI CoGetCallerTID(DWORD *tid)
 {
-    FIXME("stub!\n");
-    return E_NOTIMPL;
+    struct tlsdata *tlsdata;
+    struct apartment *apt;
+
+    TRACE("%p\n", tid);
+
+    if (!tid) return E_INVALIDARG;
+    if (FAILED(com_get_tlsdata(&tlsdata))) return E_OUTOFMEMORY;
+    if (!(apt = tlsdata->apt)) return CO_E_NOTINITIALIZED;
+
+    switch (TLS_CALLER_KIND( tlsdata ))
+    {
+    case CALLER_INPROC:   /* an STA's caller: its thread, the MTA: 0 */
+        *tid = TLS_CALLER_TID( tlsdata );
+        return S_OK;
+    case CALLER_REMOTE:   /* another process: no apartment to name */
+        *tid = 0;
+        return S_FALSE;
+    default:              /* no incoming call: the caller is the apartment of this thread */
+        *tid = apt->multi_threaded ? 0 : GetCurrentThreadId();
+        return S_OK;
+    }
 }
 
